# CHARON — Trivy CVE Suppression
# Each entry is a conscious, documented acceptance of risk.
# Reviewed: 2026-10-01

# ── pdfjs-dist ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CVE-2024-4367 — Arbitrary JavaScript execution in PDF.js (HIGH)
# Affected image: ubuntu-pdf-sandbox (Dockerfile.pdf-agent)
#
# Accepted: this CVE describes a browser-facing attack where a malicious PDF
# can execute arbitrary JS in the PDF.js viewer. In our sandbox, executing the
# JavaScript embedded in PDFs is the INTENTIONAL behaviour: pdf_runner.js
# extracts and runs every JS block in a sandboxed Node vm specifically to
# trigger syscalls that strace can observe. The "vulnerability" is our feature.
# The blast radius is bounded by: isolated K8s Job, Calico NetworkPolicy
# deny-all egress, non-root UID 10001, read-only rootfs.
CVE-2024-4367

# ── libssl3 (Ubuntu 22.04) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CVE-2026-45447 — Heap Use-After-Free in OpenSSL PKCS7_verify() (HIGH)
# Affected images: ubuntu-sandbox, ubuntu-pdf-sandbox
#
# Accepted: exploiting this CVE requires completing a full TLS handshake with
# a malicious peer. Both sandbox images run under a Calico NetworkPolicy with
# deny-all egress (charon.io/role=analysis), so no outbound TLS connections
# can be established from inside the analysis pod. Attack surface = zero.
CVE-2026-45447

# ── urllib3 (Python, sandbox agents) ────────────────────────────────────────
# urllib3==2.2.1 is installed in ubuntu-sandbox and ubuntu-pdf-sandbox as a
# dependency of the Python analysis agent. All four CVEs are decompression-bomb
# or cross-origin redirect attacks that require urllib3 to make HTTP requests to
# an attacker-controlled server. Both sandbox images run under a Calico
# NetworkPolicy with deny-all egress (charon.io/role=analysis), making these
# attack vectors unreachable from inside the analysis pod.
#
# CVE-2025-66418 — unbounded decompression chain → resource exhaustion
CVE-2025-66418
# CVE-2025-66471 — streaming API mishandles highly compressed data
CVE-2025-66471
# CVE-2026-21441 — decompression-bomb safeguard bypass via HTTP redirects
CVE-2026-21441
# CVE-2026-44431 — information disclosure via cross-origin redirect header forwarding
CVE-2026-44431
# CVE-2026-97687 — HTTPS proxy TLS config override -> traffic interception (fixed 2.8.0) (HIGH)
# CVE-2026-97689 — DoS via unbounded memory in the chunk parser (fixed 2.8.0) (HIGH)
# Same class: both require urllib3 to drive outbound HTTP to an attacker peer.
# Sandbox agents have deny-all egress; llm-layer reaches vLLM via httpx, not
# urllib3 (it only shows up via an inaccurate third-party SBOM there).
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689

# ── starlette (FastAPI dependency, core-backend) ─────────────────────────────
# starlette==0.46.2 is pulled in by fastapi in the charon-core-backend image.
# Not fixable without dropping FastAPI: even the latest FastAPI (0.128) pins
# `starlette<1.0.0`, so the fixes that live in starlette 1.x cannot be installed.
# Exploitability in our context is low: core-backend serves only POST /analyze +
# a verdict WebSocket — no StaticFiles / Range file responses / UNC path serving,
# and the upload endpoint enforces its own 35 MB size cap before parsing. The
# ingress is the browser extension (not the public Internet). Revisit when
# FastAPI supports starlette 1.x, then bump to fix all three.
#
# CVE-2025-62727 — DoS via Range header merging (fixed starlette 0.49.1) (HIGH)
CVE-2025-62727
# CVE-2026-48818 — SSRF + NTLM credential theft via UNC paths (fixed 1.1.0) (HIGH)
CVE-2026-48818
# CVE-2026-54283 — request.form() limits silently ignored (fixed 1.3.1) (HIGH)
CVE-2026-54283

# ── pip vendored libs (llm-layer) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# python:3.14-slim ships pip 26.2.1, which vendors msgpack and setuptools under
# pip/_vendor/. Trivy reads pip/_vendor/vendor.txt and reports both as fixable,
# but neither is installed as a distribution and neither can be upgraded: the
# versions are frozen inside pip itself and 26.2.1 is the latest release, so no
# `pip install --upgrade` changes what vendor.txt declares.
#
# Not exploitable here: the vendored code only ever runs when pip runs, and
# nothing in the image invokes pip after build — the container starts
# `python -m llm_layer` as UID 10003 and installs nothing at runtime.
# Revisit when a pip release refreshes its vendor set.
#
# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 — msgpack 1.1.2 out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse (HIGH)
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools 70.3.0 path traversal in PackageIndex (HIGH)
CVE-2025-47273

# ── openssl / libssl (sandbox images, runtime) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Affected images: ubuntu-sandbox, ubuntu-pdf-sandbox (ubuntu 22.04),
# sandbox-consumer (debian 13.7).
#
# Accepted: both CVEs act on attacker-controlled TLS/QUIC/DTLS traffic. The
# detonation agents run under a Calico NetworkPolicy with deny-all egress
# (charon.io/role=analysis) -> no outbound TLS at all. The consumer only opens
# client connections to known in-cluster services (Kafka, MinIO, API server);
# it never terminates DTLS/QUIC nor talks to an attacker peer. Fixed in the next
# OS package bump -> revisit on base rebuild.
#
# CVE-2026-84782 — information disclosure via DTLS handshake retransmission (HIGH)
CVE-2026-84782
# CVE-2026-75804 — DoS via unenforced QUIC connection flow control (HIGH)
CVE-2026-75804

# ── libpcre2 (sandbox-consumer, debian) ────────────────────────────────────────
# CVE-2026-103111 — out-of-bounds write via a crafted regular expression (HIGH)
#
# Accepted: exploiting this needs an ATTACKER-CONTROLLED regex. The consumer
# only compiles its own fixed patterns (job labels, parsing); no sample input is
# ever used as a regex. Fixed in libpcre2 deb13u3 -> revisit on base rebuild.
CVE-2026-103111
